{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791883004,"nonce":"mr84mQq0hgTuMce5hCMMS5H+Bw0=","title":"Anchor top-layer controls to scrolled trigger coordinates","message":"Select.show anchors its list to LayoutTree.getBounds(button.node), which reports layout coordinates before ancestor scroll offsets. The editor Animation clip trigger renders at Y about 301 while its dropdown opens around Y 521. Tooltip and Floating use the same layout bounds.\n\nFocused ChimpMonk reproducer: repro/ashui_scrolled_select/Repro.hx. Nested horizontal/vertical scrolling gives expected list position (40,166); current AshUI places it at (80,296). It fails the independent coordinate assertion. A temporary overlay of /tmp/chimpmonk-popup-anchor.patch passes ordinary and virtual Select placement and keyboard selection/dismissal, with matching (40,166) coordinates. Captures: /tmp/chimpmonk-scrolled-select-before and /tmp/chimpmonk-scrolled-select-after.\n\nPrepared change adds LayoutTree.getScrolledBounds without changing getBounds semantics, makes Scroll.at optionally tree-scoped, and uses the helper for Select, Tooltip and Floating anchors. Patch changes five Haxe files and no native ABI. Required sibling-change approval is pending; Inspector regression now explicitly asserts alignment after scrolling. Cover unscrolled anchors, horizontal/nested scrolling, ordinary/virtual lists, popup edge flipping and multiple layout trees.","files":null}]}